Sorry about the late reply.  I miss read your message as "by Wednesday
night".

1. The title is not quite exact.  When I think of interactive, the first
thing that comes to mind is some 3D stuff.  The title also does not
capture the multi-stream stuff.  How about something like "Supporting
Multi-Stream DTV Time Shifting".  Actually this one is horrible :)

2. Sec 1, Par 1, Sen 2.  "raise" -> "enables"

3. Sec 1, Par 2, last sen. Could move (...) to before the "." since a VCR
cannot filter out contents or customizes.

4. Sec 1, Par 3, first sen.  Maybe change to "To support viewing
interactivity, we have proposed a receiver-based architecture."  3rd
sentence, "The economical caching", this phrase doesn't make sense.  I
think you should also talk about DRAM in this par., like why it is used
and how it affects total costs, because in the next par. you mention how
you can "virtually eliminate the DRAM constrain", but a lay reader (like
me) would not know that DRAM poses a constrain.  Maybe something like "To
support viewing interactivity, we have proposed a receiver-based
architecture[3,4].  A receiver in this architecture is equipped with a
DRAM buffer and a large hard disk.  The speed of the DRAM and the
economics of large inexpensive disk, together with the random access
nature of these memories, enables a multimedia receiver to time shift
large amount of data.  (maybe this sentence can be replaced with one that
talks about how DRAM makes things simple, but is too expensive, thus the
goal of limiting the amount of DRAM is a very worthy one)".

5. Sec 1, Par 4. I like your examples of how multi-streams caching can be
used, but both examples could also use multiple single stream caching
devices, rather than a single box that supports multiple streams.  I would
add a third example, where the multiple streams are part of a single
program, thus you must cache all streams by one device.  Examples include
branching movies and multi-view sports broadcast.

6. Sec 1, last par, 1st sen.  "(the standard DTV bitrate)" ->(a standard
definition DTV bitstream).  I would also add "(up to 81x)" after
"high-speed" in this sentence.  If I stop reading here, it would be nice
to give me one of your key results.

7. Sec 3, par 1, last sen.  This sentence is misleading.  ATVEF is based
on IP, it uses the MPEG2 transport stream, rather than the MPEG2 video
encoding standard.  How about "We discuss the k-file scheme in the context
of DTV video encoding standard, MPEG2.".  I think this is enough since
pretty much everybody knows the importance of MPEG2, and it is the only
high bitrate standard (I think).

8. Sec 6, Par 1.  Extra "o" on the first line.

9. I like your traffic light and stop sign analogy, but that is true only
for traffic lights without car sensors.  For most of the traffic lights
around my parents' house, traffice light will always beat stop sign.

I think this paper is a sure acceptance :)

Milton










